Implemented and pushed for review: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1500

FULL reference set found (Serena + a string grep — the string grep is what caught the DC sites, since attribute injection is exactly what the LSP cannot resolve):

Production, all four now gone:
1. outbound_field_diff.py — the core injection (try/except AttributeError,TypeError: pass), replaced by a bound closure passed as an argument;
2. adapters/jira/backend.py — Cloud getattr discovery -> declared parameter;
3. adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:118 — DC getattr discovery -> declared parameter;
4. adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:331 — DC constructor injection onto self.outbound with a type: ignore[attr-defined] -> a declared _DCOutbound constructor parameter.

Plus the intermediate hop the original plan missed: resolve_assignee is called inside diff_canonical_fields, not at the injection point, so the resolver had to be threaded through that function too.

Sites ONLY the string grep found (Serena's semantic set returned the two resolve_assignee implementers and the port, and nothing for the attribute itself):
- both DC sites above (the receiver is untyped/attribute-injected, so the LSP binds nothing);
- tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_user_identity_heldout.py:148, which built its six-state parity expectation via backend.outbound._assignee_resolver = ...;
- outbound_differ.py:384, a nested local function that merely shares the name — deliberately left alone (it is not a collaborator smuggled onto an object; the new structural test keys on attribute ASSIGNMENT, not the bare name, so it stays legal).

Test doubles that implement resolve_assignee also had to accept the new keyword (4 files under tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/).

Design point recorded for posterity: DC's resolver is bound at CONSTRUCTION to the deployment client (no jira_key), while the core's is per-issue. resolve_assignee prefers the explicit parameter and falls back to the constructor one — which reproduces the old behaviour exactly, since the core injection used to overwrite the constructor-set attribute.

Local gates: make lint, make typecheck, and the full suite (11068 passed, 148 skipped) all green.
